      <div class="WordSection1">
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">Hi Mr.
            White,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><o:p> </o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">I do not
            have enough information to determine if any of your four
            requests qualify for facilitated dispute resolution.
            Moreover, ORS 192.468 states, “Consistent with ORS 192.464
            and rules adopted thereunder, the Public Records Advocate
            possesses sole discretion over the conduct of facilitated
            dispute resolution sessions.”<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><o:p> </o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">Facilitated
            dispute resolution is merely mediation. I do not have the
            authority to order outcomes in public records requests. As
            such, whether we are assisting through facilitated dispute
            resolution or other, less formal forms of mediation, I need
            to understand the parameters of a disputed request, and have
            the cooperation of all parties.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><o:p> </o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">At the
            moment, I have none of these things. As mentioned
            previously, I am also one of two people in a state agency
            that received nearly 400 individual requests for assistance
            such as yours last year while striving to address them all
            in a timely matter. Please keep in mind that mediating
            disputed requests is only one of the forms of assistance we
            offer on public records matters and, as such, are engaged in
            those other duties too.
            <o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><o:p> </o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">Therefore,
            we assist requesters with one disputed public records
            request at a time to assure equitable access to all of those
            seeking our services. We also require answers to our
            questions and agreeable interactions that permit the free
            flow of information.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><o:p> </o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">With this in
            mind, are you interested in working with us along the terms
            I outlined? If so, with which request do you wish to begin?<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><o:p> </o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">On the other
            hand, if you find these terms unacceptable, then we will not
            be able to work with you further and I wish you the best of
            luck in your endeavors.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><o:p> </o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt">Kind
            regards,<o:p></o:p></span></p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:11.0pt"><o:p> </o:p></span></p>
